alse,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"C042\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States the 75-day period under Rule 485(a)(2) for a new series, notes acceleration and other provisions, says the clock is not an end-to-end launch guarantee, and treats initial trust registration as a different regime rather than applying the 75-day clock to it.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Optional point. The answer does not say shares cannot be sold before effectiveness and gives no filed example. This omission does not reduce the grade.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says the clock covers registration-statement effectiveness, not completion of launch work, and lists exchange listing, seed capital, operational readiness and required regulatory steps. The optional 95-day designated-date limit is omitted, which does not reduce the grade.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"\\\"generally becomes effective no earlier than 60 days after its initial filing under Investment Company Act § 8(a), absent acceleration\\\" — This is a material misstatement. Investment Company Act § 8(a) governs notification of registration (Form N-8A), which is effective on receipt and has no 60-day clock. Securities Act § 8(a) gives a 20-day default for a registration statement, which is commonly extended by a delaying amendment until the SEC declares it effective. The answer gives the wrong period and the wrong statutory source for the initial-registration distinction the question asks for. It is not the listed central error, because it does not apply the 75-day Rule 485 clock to the new trust.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Both required points are fully covered and there is no central error. The answer does not apply the 75-day clock to initial trust registration and does not call it a launch guarantee. However, its account of the requested initial-registration distinction gives a false 60-day period and attributes it to Investment Company Act § 8(a). Under the scoring rule, a material local falsehood caps the grade at partial.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":5658,"type":"result","duration_ms":11252,"uuid":"4da089ab-f61b-4789-a51b-937846af6a17","ttft_stream_ms":1474,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1474,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
